  "prefLabel": "Ins 2604.14 Third Party Approval and Endorsement",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Ins 2604.14 Third Party Approval and Endorsement.\n\n(a) An advertisement shall not state or imply that a governmental agency has approved an insurer or a policy, or has examined an insurer's financial condition and found it satisfactory, unless such is the fact.\n\n(b) An advertisement shall not state or imply that any individual, group, society, association, or other organization has approved or endorsed an insurer or a policy unless such is the fact.\n\nSource. #9333, eff 12-5-08; ss by #11173, eff 12-5-16",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/ins2600.html"
}
